Package: craftos-system
Version: 0.1
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: systemd-zram-generator, systemd-oomd, fwupd, gnome-software-plugin-fwupd, firewalld, btrfs-progs, snapper, btrfs-assistant, grub-btrfs, inotify-tools, initramfs-tools, gstreamer1.0-libav, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad
Recommends: ffmpeg
Maintainer: nu-stats <j.stowell@northeastern.edu>
Homepage: https://github.com/nu-stats/craftos
Description: CraftOS system defaults (the Fedora-style extras)
 What makes CraftOS feel like Fedora under the hood, on Debian:
  - zram: compressed swap in RAM (zstd, up to half of RAM, at most 8 GB);
  - systemd-oomd: stops runaway programs before the desktop freezes;
  - firmware updates from the Software app (fwupd / LVFS);
  - firewall on by default (firewalld, "CraftOS" zone: nothing comes in
    except printer and file-sharing discovery);
  - Btrfs snapshots before and after every apt run (snapper), the Btrfs
    Assistant app to browse and restore them, and a GRUB menu to boot into
    an older snapshot (grub-btrfs);
  - audio and video codecs.
